            <li><strong className="text-foreground">Soccer Career: clubs go up and down now.</strong> From the 2026-27 season in <Link to="/soccer-career" className="text-primary hover:underline">Soccer Career</Link>, clubs move between the top two divisions in England, Germany, France, Italy and Spain. Finish in the drop zone and your club really goes down, so next season you are playing in the second division, and a top finish down there brings you back up. Your season summary and the Season Centre say so when your club moves, the clubs that go down or come up are the ones you see in those places of the final table, and transfer offers follow the divisions as they stand in your career. If a bad injury ends your season early, or you sit a year out, the league still finishes without you: your club can move then too, and your season log tells you. It is your career's own made up future, not a prediction: straight swaps with no playoffs, three clubs each way in England, Italy and Spain and two in Germany and France. Spain's second division plays with 20 of its real 22 clubs, because the two reserve sides are left out. A career already past 2026 picks this up from its next season, and seasons before 2026 are untouched.</li>
